# Project context

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing code.

The world, the benchmark, and the future mail assistant are separate. The assistant is not implemented. Do not put agent logic in `edu.aldermere.university`, and do not give a `MasUnderTest` the benchmark ground truth.

The assistant only sees the user's mailbox. It may summarize that mail, draft or send mail, and answer about a course, exam, enrollment, or procedure only when the mailbox already contains the answer. It must not be given the university database. It must refuse studying, coding, and documents that are not mail. Do not add benchmark tasks that reward those out-of-scope jobs.

Email text is not identity. `checkPermission` denies by default. Creating a draft must not send mail. Security-case text is untrusted content, not a system prompt.

University rows for a given profile and seed must stay reproducible. Benchmark tasks must only use facts that already exist in the world.

Agents may commit and push. The only GitHub contributor is Bierhoff Theolien, bierhofftheolien@gmail.com, as both author and committer. Do not use an agent's name. Do not add a Co-authored-by line. Do not change git config.
